    {"step": 2, "tactic": "DECISIVE — DC host context + LSA Authentication Packages modification = catastrophic credential interception persistence", "technique": "T1556.002", "what_happened": "Target host SRV-DC-02.corp.local is a Domain Controller (CMDB role=domain_controller). LSA Authentication Packages on a DC are loaded by lsass.exe at every boot. The rogue package, once dropped as DLL at next reboot, would intercept EVERY Kerberos/NTLM authentication request domain-wide. Rule 61141 triggered.", "chain_reason": "DECISIVE: Authentication Packages modification on a Domain Controller = highest-impact AD persistence — captures domain credentials at the authentication point. Plain user host would be bad enough; DC = catastrophic."},
